roshi exiting  these semi-finals following a loss not  with a sense of disappointment or shame  but instead with a feeling of deep  comfort knowing that the future is  bright with these impressive individuals  leading the charge and speaking of those  leading the charge goku's fight with  krillin is something to behold the  camaraderie demonstrated both off and on  the fighting stage is heartwarming but  the respect each competitor shows each  other is remarkable with krillin asking  goku not to hold back or he won't ever  forgive him and goku claiming that this  is the most fun fight he's ever had  impressive in both the manga and anime  making full use of their respective  mediums the philosophy surrounding this  fight as i mentioned is fantastic but  once again it is yet another fight that  has some stupendous toriyama  choreography exploiting every angle and  utilizing some unique uses for the  kamehameha from both competitors goku  using it as a booster to give his  punches more power and krillin using it  defensively to create an opening for him  to grab his tail once again leading into  the strategic workarounds in his persona  unluckily for krillin however in the  three years since they last saw each  other goku removed that weakness and  once that option was removed krillin was  simply outmatched by the young fighter  goku emerges victorious with a nice bit  of writing between the referee and goku  to cap everything off at the end the  referee says to goku the next batch is  the championship round would you like to  take a break and goku responds puzzled  and i don't care goku very much valued  that fight but it by no means pushed him  at all this next fight should be a fun  one the finals sun goku versus 10  shinhan  the beginning of this fight is filled  with strategy encounters initially  losing early on goku impressed with  tenshihan's power and toughness decides  to push harder and harder getting into  an apparent advantageous position early  on as tin shinhan in the air is primed  for kamehameha but goku chooses not to  use it it's subtle but i love this  indication that he's taken on board  different pieces of advice he's been  offered growing up as a young kid he was  criticized for not thinking things  through and charging in head-on but  right here you can see the strategy he's  employing he's aware that this opponent  is powerful and has the ability to fly  he might dodge it he thinks this fight  will be a long one and he needs that  energy towards the beginning of this  fight tension on particularly when it  comes to the vanishing technique goku  uses and has used against krillin in the  past he immediately recognizes the move  from the prior fight and counters it  immediately but as the fight wears on  goku implements similar applied learning  to the tao ken or solar flare if you've  seen the dub immediately snatching roshi  sunglasses allowing him to land a heavy  blow onto tenshinhan i love choreography  like this it's massively fun and i love  the pervasive use of callbacks to  earlier points in the arc and further  setting this fight apart every fight  from the qualifiers up until now have  been relatively short lasting no longer  than a chapter or two and so narratively  because this is given ample time to  breathe it feels all the more  significant and huge as a final it feels  like a massive occasion the fight isn't  over in an instant it lasts long enough  to tell a story and for us as an  audience to feel the rhythm of that  story tien's impressed tien gains the  upper hand goku's impressed goku gains  the upper hand but the real overarching  story concerning this encounter and  really this entire tournament has  concerned itself with the struggle for  tin shinhan's soul during roshi's fight  with tin shinhan a large part of it  focused on roshi trying to instill some  sort of lesson in the young fighter  recognizing that he has so much  potential as a martial artist despite  his horrible master and during this  fight with goku his allegiances are  tested in ways he never anticipated  [Music]  this is an important moment not simply  because it finally creates a moment for  attention hunt to distance himself from  the crane school but instead because it  sets in motion a trend whereby the  villains secure their own downfall  personally i love this narrative choice  and it is by far and away my favorite  narrative tool to dispose of villains  not just in dragon ball but the wider  world i first noticed this technique  used in the film tarzan as a child when  clayton the story's villain through his  blind hate-filled pursuit of tarzan  inadvertently hangs himself despite  tarzan's greatest efforts to prevent him  from doing so it's a simple but  massively effective tool that highlights  the villain's flaws and amplifies the  hero's virtues and in dragon ball later  this technique will be used to bring  about the downfall of the series two  most iconic villains and right here in  classic dragon ball we see the impetus  for this narrative technique master  crane demands that tenshinhan kill goku  not understanding his pupil or the honor  he wants to conduct this match with and  despite his screams for murder death and  revenge he gets a kamehameha courtesy of  master roshi sending him flying i love  this scene following this tenshinhan  brings to light techniques goku could  never have imagined sprouting two  additional arms creating instances where  goku can't defend himself but primed us  as an audience for swerves like goku  using his tail as a fifth appendage to  even the odds this is such a fun and  creative fight and honestly it pains me  that we don't see more creative  implementation of maneuverings in modern  dragon ball fights they offer so much  entertainment and to think that these  are concepts or relics of a bygone era  is honestly quite sad everyone nowadays  wants their latest transformations or  flashy beams but back here we had  legitimate strategy using moves never  before seen in the story it makes the  world feel so incredibly colorful that  is until the climax to this fight  for when tenshinhan bellows the name of  this technique the color is zapped from  the faces of chiaotsu krillin and roshi  respectively  terrified both for goku and tenshinhan  there are so many ups and downs to this  fight at this point it's clearly the  most intense in the series made evident  by the number of story beats and the  fact that the stage has been  disintegrated but narrowly having  escaped by jumping high into the air  goku remains tenshinhan is drained and  goku readies one last kamehameha  the one he saved for such an occasion  earlier in the conflict but instead  knowing that tin shinon has an answer  for that technique as made evident in  his prior encounters goku once again  finds a creative use for the blast  knowing that he can't fly fast enough to  evade a blow propelled by the force of a  kamehameha goku launches himself like a  rocket towards the weary fighter they  both hurtled towards the ground and the  first to touch down loses goku manages  to expel just enough energy to put  himself above tension and when  [Music]  first reading this i was stunned given  the subject matter and philosophy of the  prior world tournament it stood to  reason that he would likely lose the  21st tenkaichi budokai i mean come on it  was his first and that was the lesson of  the outing at the end of the day but to  lose it again for a second time at the  finish line i was stunned every fight  leading up to this encounter had goku  like a powerhouse steamrolling through  the competition and to have him lose  here albeit in a questionable manner was  stunning for me to read first time  through the fight was incredible it had  some interesting narrative choices and  was the single best visual fight  toriyama had produced to date in my  estimation but somewhat remarkably this  arc wouldn't be remembered for this  fight but instead remembered for its  aftermath  [Music]  [Music]  the unthinkable has happened a terrific  tournament has ended in tragedy next  week i will cover what many consider to  be the very best original dragon ball  has to offer when i dive into the king  piccolo arc and beyond i'll see you  there  [Music]  foreign
 

